  "status": "OFFLINE EXACT-BYTE VERIFIED - ON-CAR TEST REQUIRED",
  "tested": false,
  "verification": "V17 exact installed-byte checks cover later-angle arbitration, native fault priority, knock transaction freeze and native window/reply/sample recovery, retained learning, RAM coexistence, configured migration, diagnostic recovery and full-stack boot/reset. This is bounded emulator evidence; bench and on-car validation remain required.",
  "title": "Ignition Cut",
  "user_description": "Independent ignition-cut limiter with RPM hysteresis, optional fixed injector pulse width and an optional fixed ignition angle in a configurable RPM region below the cut limit. Provides shared timing and combustion-observation recovery for Launch Control V17.",
  "description": "MS41.0 Ignition Cut V17 retains V16 runtime ownership and calibrations. The active limiter angle is the later of the requested absolute angle and native protected timing. Native input and knock-sensor faults retain their veto; learned knock corrections are never cleared. Knock learning waits through patch cut/retard activity and native window/reply/sample recovery using D805-D80B. Exact compatible predecessor pairs migrate together and retain configured calibration bytes.",
  "target": "MS41.0",
